# 102. Binary Tree Level Order Traversal

## APPROACH: BINARY TREE LEVEL ORDER TRAVERSAL

Idea:
Tree ko horizontally level-by-level traverse karna hai (Breadth First Search - BFS).
Pehle Level 0 (root), fir Level 1 (root ke children), fir Level 2, and so on.
Har level ke elements ko ek separate list me store karna hai.

--------------------------------------------------

APPROACH (Iterative / BFS using Queue)

1. Edge Case:
   Agar `root == null` hai, seedha empty list return kar do.

2. Ek Queue (`Queue<TreeNode>`) banao aur root ko insert (`offer`) karo.

3. Jab tak queue empty na ho jaye (`while(!queue.isEmpty())`):
   - Current level ka size nikaalo: `levelSize = queue.size()`.
     (Yeh step critical hai: isse pata chalta hai ki current level me kitne nodes hain).
   - Ek temporary list banao: `currLevel`.

4. Exactly `levelSize` times loop chalao (`for(int i = 0; i < levelSize; i++)`):
   - Queue se node bahar nikaalo (`poll`).
   - Uski value `currLevel` me add karo.
   - Agar uska `left` child exist karta hai, usse queue me dalo.
   - Agar uska `right` child exist karta hai, usse queue me dalo.

5. Loop khatam hone par `currLevel` list ko main `result` list me add kar do.

6. Final `result` return karo.

--------------------------------------------------

EXAMPLE

Tree:
      3
     / \
    9   20
        /  \
       15   7

Dry Run:
- Initial: Queue = [3], result = []

Level 1:
- levelSize = 1
- Poll 3 -> currLevel = [3]
- Queue me 9 aur 20 add huye -> Queue = [9, 20]
- result = [[3]]

Level 2:
- levelSize = 2
- Poll 9 -> currLevel = [9] (9 ke children null hain)
- Poll 20 -> currLevel = [9, 20] (20 ke children 15 aur 7 queue me gaye)
- Queue = [15, 7]
- result = [[3], [9, 20]]

Level 3:
- levelSize = 2
- Poll 15 -> currLevel = [15]
- Poll 7 -> currLevel = [15, 7]
- Queue empty
- result = [[3], [9, 20], [15, 7]]

--------------------------------------------------

WHY QUEUE?

- Level order traversal FIFO (First In, First Out) principle follow karta hai.
- Jo node pehle level par aayi hai, uske children ko baad ke levels ke liye queue ke end me daalna hota hai.

--------------------------------------------------

COMPLEXITY

N = Total number of nodes in tree
W = Maximum width of binary tree (maximum nodes at any level)

Time:
O(N) -> Har node queue me exactly ek baar insert aur ek baar remove hoti hai.

Space:
O(N) ya O(W) -> Queue me at most kisi level ke saare nodes rahenge.
Full binary tree ke case me last level par lagbhag N/2 nodes hote hain, toh queue space O(N) ho sakti hai.
*(Excluding output result list)*

--------------------------------------------------

INTERVIEW POINT

- Size freeze karna sabse important trick hai: `int levelSize = queue.size()` loop se pehle store karna padta hai, kyunki loop ke andar hum next level ke nodes push kar rahe hote hain jisse queue ka size change hota rehta hai.
- Follow-up variations:
  1. Zigzag Level Order Traversal (alternate levels reverse karke).
  2. Right/Left view of Binary Tree (har level ka last ya first element pick karke).
  3. Average/Max value of each level.

--------------------------------------------------

# CODE:

import java.util.*;

/**
 * Definition for a binary tree node.
 * public class TreeNode {
 *     int val;
 *     TreeNode left;
 *     TreeNode right;
 *     TreeNode() {}
 *     TreeNode(int val) { this.val = val; }
 *     TreeNode(int val, TreeNode left, TreeNode right) {
 *         this.val = val;
 *         this.left = left;
 *         this.right = right;
 *     }
 * }
 */
class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> levelOrder(TreeNode root) {
        List<List<Integer>> result = new ArrayList<>();
        if (root == null) {
            return result;
        }

        Queue<TreeNode> queue = new LinkedList<>();
        queue.offer(root);

        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {
            int levelSize = queue.size();
            List<Integer> currLevel = new ArrayList<>();

            for (int i = 0; i < levelSize; i++) {
                TreeNode currNode = queue.poll();
                currLevel.add(currNode.val);

                if (currNode.left != null) {
                    queue.offer(currNode.left);
                }
                if (currNode.right != null) {
                    queue.offer(currNode.right);
                }
            }
            result.add(currLevel);
        }

        return result;
    }
}
